Subject: KTM, new option


Dear Roustam,

  After some break (I put my wife into hospital)
I try to continue calculations for KTM and it is 
VERY desirable your help.
  There are some changes in parameters and 
redistribution the work between NIIEFA and LSZ.

  Firstly, windows for I.A.Kovan antennaes lead
to decreasing the number of toroidal coils: 24 --> 16.
In the result for the same level of TF ripples at the
plasma end (0.5%) it is necessary to increase the
radius of external toroidal leg up to 1.7 m (at the 
middle part of toroidal coil). So, part of poloidal coils 
are also moved to higher radiuses. The minimum 
changes in the PF coils position can be the following:

                 R, cm          Z, cm
PF1             44              155
PF2             64              155
PF3             123             155
PF4             175             100
PF5             175             50
PF6             175            -50
PF7             175            -100
PF8             123            -155
PF9             64             -155
PF10            44             -150
PF11            22.5          +-150

By another words R position of PF5-PF8 is slightly
shifted.

  Secondly, there are some changes to the plasma 
scenario dIp/dt = 3 MA/s...

  Some data of this scenario can be the following:

time,s      .01  .06  .11  .16  .21  .26  .31  .35  10
ne20        .15  .20  .25 .35 .50 .50  .50 .50  .50
a,m         .18  .28   .40 .40 .40 .40  .40 .40  .40
R,m        1.02 .92   .90 .85 .80 .80  .80 .80  .80
k              1    1.05  1.2  1.3 1.4  1.5   1.7  1.7  1.7
delta          0    0      0  .05 .1    .15   .2    .2   .2
gamOx,%   1     1      1     1    1     1     1      1     1      
Paux,MW   0    0     0     0   0    0     0     5    5

Here gamOx - impurity (Oxygen) content.
Data in the Table are linearly interpolated between
time points.

For this initial data OD scenario was calculated.
Its preliminary data were:
<T> = 1.03 (To = 2.2) keV; tayE = 0.02 s; for CS flux
total change 2 V.s the discharge duration is about 2 s
(from the breakdown to end of plasma current plateau).
Start - from inboard. Plasma voltage during auxiliary
heating is about 0.5 V. Safety factor q95 is about 4 
during the all scenario. beta N is up to 2.1 . Bootstrap
current fraction is about .25-.3 .

It is very desirable to formulate any comments to this
plasma scenario and, may be change it.

>From my mind - what is necessary to do firstly and
quickly:

1). Scenario of PF currents in characteristical points of
scenario - it is VERY necessary for NIIEFA designers.
(The PF currents at the time point of plasma breakdown
are also necessary; at this time moment the level of
stray field must be about 5 - 10 Gauss in the region
with radiuses R = 1.0 m , a = 0.2 m, Z = 0 .

I don't have ANY PF coils scenario for KTM.

2). Special question is related to the divertor configuration
creation at the plasma current. It is necessary to say
that the position of vacuum chamber in radial direction now 
is from R = 0.38 m up to R = 1.24 m . It is very 
important to answer the question: is the DIVERTOR 
configuration created for given geometry (not only limiter 
configuration)? If it will be any problems - please let me know. 
Estimations of SOL thickness for KTM conditions leads to 
values 2-3 cm. If will be large difficulties it may be 
necessary to input the special short solenoid  for the 
plasma form creation at the inboard.

3). Now the struggle between designers about plasma centre
position (Zaxis coordinate) take place. For the divertor 
program it is desirable to have Zaxiz about 20 cm ) so
the plasma axis is 20 cm shifted to the upper parts of the 
vacuum chamber and there is more place for divertor 
placing. For antennas may be better Zaxis = 0,
the same may be from the point of PF currents minimisation. 
Who will be the wimmer in this struggle is not known now.
But it will be very desirable after points (punkts) 1). and 2). to
calculate the PF scenario also for Zaxis = 20 cm at the plasma 
current plateau ( for this scenario plasma is started from the 
symmetrical position with Zaxis = 0).

Best regards, Anatoly




